# This file ships with the boilerplate because the boilerplate becomes the
# project root, so it is in place before the first agent writes anything.
# B01 owns it (REQ-FND-13).
#
# Read the "never ignore" section at the bottom before adding a line. Two of the
# obvious entries would break the build, and one would destroy this project's
# conformity evidence.

# ── Build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
target/
**/target/
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp

# ── Installer and release output ────────────────────────────────────────────
*.msi
*.msix
*.wixpdb
*.wixobj
dist/
staging/

# ── Test and capture output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
build/screenshots/*.tmp.png
tests/visual/**/*.actual.png
*.profraw

# ── Signing material. These are the lines that matter ───────────────────────
# REQ-REL-04: the signing key never enters a build log, a repository, or an
# unencrypted CI variable. REQ-UPD-02's whole trust chain rests on the update
# signing key being secret; a git history is not something you can un-leak.
#
# NOTE the asymmetry: the *private* halves are ignored, the *public* halves are
# committed on purpose — crates/update/keys/*.pub is include_str!'d into the
# binary (REQ-UPD-03), so ignoring it breaks the build outright.
*.pfx
*.p12
*.snk
*.key
*.sec
minisign.key
!**/*.pub
secrets/

# ── Anything JavaScript that shows up alongside (docs tooling, CI helpers) ──
node_modules/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Local and OS noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEVER ignore these. Each looks like build output and is not:
#
#   build/          The gate verdicts, the intake, the human's H1 design
#                   approval and the cost ledger. compliance/cra/obligations-matrix.md
#                   cites build/gates/*.md as Annex I II(3) evidence at the
#                   strongest tier, on the grounds that an auditor can check a
#                   path. An auditor cannot check a path that is not in the
#                   repository. Only build/screenshots/*.tmp.png is ignored.
#   mockups/        The compiled styling proofs. The winning mockup stays
#                   in-tree as the reference the design is checked against
#                   (REQ-MOC-08), and the ones that lost stay as the record of
#                   what was rejected. Their target/ dirs are covered above.
#   crates/update/keys/*.pub   The embedded update public keys (REQ-UPD-03).
#                   include_str! resolves these at compile time — ignore them
#                   and the crate does not build.
#   crates/update/tests/fixtures/   The wrong-key, mutated-signature and
#                   tampered-artefact fixtures. They are committed deliberately
#                   because minisign-verify cannot sign, so they are generated
#                   out of band once. Regenerating them is not possible in CI.
#
# scripts/check-boilerplate.sh fails if any of them is ignored.
